Rāvaṇa claims brotherhood with humbled Kubēra --- Rāvaṇa claims gods wind sun and rivers fear him --- Rāvaṇa describes moated golden Laṅkā full of demons --- Rāvaṇa offers human and divine pleasures with him --- Rāvaṇa mocks Rāma as dethroned short-lived ascetic --- Rāvaṇa warns refusal brings remorse like Urvaśī --- Sītā rebukes doomed rākṣasas under cruel king --- Sītā declares stealing Śacī survivable but not Rāma wife